     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"No single blocked step makes crownData:exfiltrate unreachable, because every route into the target has a backup. The target is an OR over vaultRead, codeRepo, dbReplica and mailArchive. mailArchive is an OR over monitoringHost, fileServer and localAdmin. monitoringHost is an OR over apiToken, vpnSession and tokenCache, and tokenCache comes straight from the exposedApi entry foothold. apiToken (workstation via phishing, plus sshKey via internet) and vpnSession (browserStore plus mailClient via vpnGateway) are also reachable, so monitoringHost survives blocking any one of its parents. fileServer is reachable via rdpLogin, which needs browserStore and ciRunner, both reachable from internet; this gives mailArchive a second independent path. If mailArchive itself is blocked, vaultRead is still reachable via hypervisor (rdpLogin AND vpnSession, both reachable). codeRepo (via printServer) and dbReplica (via serviceAccount) are also reachable. Therefore no non-foothold, non-target step is a single point of failure.\"}\n```"
    }
